<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Tools on 星双</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tags/tools/</link><description>Recent content in Tools on 星双</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:35:20 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://jzjizhe.github.io/tags/tools/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>VSCode Neovim - Prevent Output Panel from Stealing Focus</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tool/vscode-neovim---prevent-output-panel-from-stealing-focus/</link><pubDate>Wed, 29 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tool/vscode-neovim---prevent-output-panel-from-stealing-focus/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;strong>The note is generated by Opus-4.7&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="problem">Problem&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>When using the vscode-neovim extension, the VSCode Output panel automatically reveals and steals focus from the terminal whenever Neovim logs appear.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="root-cause">Root Cause&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>In &lt;code>src/messages_manager.ts&lt;/code>, the extension calls &lt;code>this.channel.show(true)&lt;/code> (which reveals and focuses the Output panel) whenever the number of lines in a Neovim message exceeds &lt;code>cmdheight&lt;/code>:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">&lt;tr>&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">1
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">2
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">3
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">4
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">5
&lt;/span>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">6
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-typescript" data-lang="typescript">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#cf222e">const&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">lineCount&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#0550ae">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">outputMsg&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">.&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">split&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">(&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#0a3069">&amp;#34;\n&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">).&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">length&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#cf222e">const&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">cmdheight&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#0550ae">=&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">(&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#cf222e">await&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#cf222e">this&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">.&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">main&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">.&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">client&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">.&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">getOption&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">(&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#0a3069">&amp;#34;cmdheight&amp;#34;&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">))&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#cf222e">as&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#cf222e">number&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">;&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#cf222e">if&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">(&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">lineCount&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#0550ae">&amp;gt;&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">cmdheight&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">)&lt;/span> &lt;span style="color:#1f2328">{&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span> &lt;span style="color:#cf222e">this&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">.&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">channel&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">.&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">show&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">(&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#cf222e">true&lt;/span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">);&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>&lt;span style="color:#1f2328">}&lt;/span>
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;ul>
&lt;li>&lt;code>cmdheight=0&lt;/code> (default when &lt;code>ext_messages&lt;/code> is enabled): every message exceeds 0 lines → Output panel steals focus on &lt;strong>every&lt;/strong> log&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;code>cmdheight=1&lt;/code>: only messages with &lt;strong>more than 1 line&lt;/strong> trigger the Output panel&lt;/li>
&lt;li>&lt;code>cmdheight=N&lt;/code>: only messages exceeding N lines trigger it&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h2 id="fix">Fix&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Set &lt;code>cmdheight=1&lt;/code> in the VSCode-specific Neovim config (&lt;code>~/.config/nvim/lua/plugins/vscode.lua&lt;/code>):&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Git 配置PAT</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/git/git-%E9%85%8D%E7%BD%AEpat/</link><pubDate>Fri, 24 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://jzjizhe.github.io/git/git-%E9%85%8D%E7%BD%AEpat/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;strong>The note is partly generated by &amp;ldquo;ChatGPT.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>The article &lt;a href="https://jzjizhe.github.io/git/proxy-set-but-ssh--t-git@github.com-still-fails/">“Proxy set, but &lt;code>ssh -T git@github.com&lt;/code> still fails”&lt;/a> explains that Git SSH cannot use an HTTP proxy and provides a solution. However, in my experience, even using that solution, network performance can be unreliable. Therefore, if you can use HTTPS for Git, I recommend switching from SSH to HTTPS directly. Below is the method to switch to HTTPS and configure a Personal Access Token (PAT) for authentication.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Proxy set, but ssh -T git@github.com fails</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/git/proxy-set-but-ssh--t-git@github.com-fails/</link><pubDate>Fri, 24 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://jzjizhe.github.io/git/proxy-set-but-ssh--t-git@github.com-fails/</guid><description>&lt;p>&lt;strong>The note is generated by ChatGPT.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="observation--proxy-set-but-ssh-still-fails">&lt;strong>Observation — Proxy set, but SSH still fails&lt;/strong>&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Although you set &lt;code>http_proxy&lt;/code> / &lt;code>https_proxy&lt;/code> (or &lt;code>all_proxy&lt;/code>), running:&lt;/p>
&lt;div class="highlight">&lt;div style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">
&lt;table style="border-spacing:0;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">&lt;tr>&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code>&lt;span style="white-space:pre;-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;margin-right:0.4em;padding:0 0.4em 0 0.4em;color:#7f7f7f">1
&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>
&lt;td style="vertical-align:top;padding:0;margin:0;border:0;;width:100%">
&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="background-color:#fff;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;">&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash">&lt;span style="display:flex;">&lt;span>ssh -T git@github.com
&lt;/span>&lt;/span>&lt;/code>&lt;/pre>&lt;/td>&lt;/tr>&lt;/table>
&lt;/div>
&lt;/div>&lt;p>still times out or fails.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="root-cause--ssh-does-not-use-the-http-proxy--key-point">&lt;strong>Root cause — SSH does NOT use the HTTP proxy&lt;/strong> (key point)&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>Terminal HTTP/SOCKS environment variables affect HTTP/HTTPS-aware programs (curl, wget, &lt;code>git clone https://…&lt;/code>, etc.), but &lt;strong>OpenSSH does not honor those variables&lt;/strong>. SSH opens a raw TCP connection and must be explicitly told to use a proxy — otherwise it tries a direct connection and gets blocked by the network/firewall.&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>Trash-cli — The Recycle Bin on Linux</title><link>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tool/trash-cli--the-recycle-bin-on-linux/</link><pubDate>Thu, 23 Oct 2025 00:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://jzjizhe.github.io/tool/trash-cli--the-recycle-bin-on-linux/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="-overview">📘 Overview&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>On Linux, the command-line tool &lt;a href="https://github.com/andreafrancia/trash-cli">&lt;code>trash-cli&lt;/code>&lt;/a> provides a &lt;strong>safe alternative to &lt;code>rm&lt;/code>&lt;/strong>, allowing you to move files to the &lt;strong>Trash&lt;/strong> instead of permanently deleting them.&lt;br>
It fully complies with the &lt;a href="https://specifications.freedesktop.org/trash-spec/latest/">FreeDesktop Trash Specification&lt;/a>, which is used by desktop environments such as GNOME and KDE.&lt;/p>
&lt;hr>
